__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local secrets for helper_agent live OpenAI tests (tests/README.md) — never committed.
.env

# Dev-only test tooling deps (package.json) — index.html itself ships with none.
node_modules/

# tests/evals/results/*.md is intentionally NOT ignored: report.md,
# conversation-log.md, tool-calls.md are committed with every PR that
# includes a live eval run, so anyone browsing the repo can see (and
# audit) the latest run's real transcript without re-running it themselves.
# Only the latest run's files are ever committed -- each write overwrites
# the previous run's content, never accumulates -- see tests/evals/README.md.

# Scratch driver scripts for long eval batches. They carry endpoint/key values
# in the environment and must never be committed -- GitHub's secret scanning
# caught exactly that once. The runner itself reads credentials from the
# environment and hardcodes nothing.
*.tmp.sh
*.tmp.mjs

# Transient per-run scratch from a live eval batch. `progress.json` is a live
# status file rewritten every turn, and `checkpoint/` is the partial transcript
# and model kept so an interrupted run is recoverable. Both are superseded by
# the run's real artifacts on a clean finish, so the repo tracks the results
# and not the machinery that produced them.
tests/evals/results/baselines/*/*/*/progress.json
tests/evals/results/baselines/*/*/*/checkpoint/

# ontology_translation domain pipeline (issue #101-#111): compile.py's/
# evaluate.py's own working output -- candidate run-N.domain.yaml/
# translation.json siblings, run-manifest.json, run.log.jsonl, and every
# eval-*/ report directory a manual pipeline run produces along the way.
# Same "repo tracks the results, not the machinery" convention as the evals
# baselines above: only the final, human-adjudicated
# reference.domain.yaml/translation.json/translation-evaluation.json/
# translation-report.md/persona.md/manual-spot-check.* land in a domain's
# folder (see brick-hvac/iof-supply-chain for the established file set) --
# the numbered candidates and intermediate eval reports that got there are
# fully reproducible from source-manifest.yaml via run_pipeline.py and would
# otherwise churn on every re-run for no reason.
ontology_translation/domains/*/run-*.domain.yaml
ontology_translation/domains/*/run-*.translation.json
ontology_translation/domains/*/run-manifest.json
ontology_translation/domains/*/run.log.jsonl
ontology_translation/domains/*/source_ir.json
ontology_translation/domains/*/eval-*/
ontology_translation/domains/*/repair-*.json
ontology_translation/domains/*/repair-out*/
ontology_translation/domains/*/reinstate-*.json
ontology_translation/domains/*/reinstate-out*/
